1
00:00:01,019 --> 00:00:00,950
Fifty-nine.

2
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,330
That's how many Honda Accords were sold
in the whole of Australia in the first

3
00:00:04,380 --> 00:00:06,510
nine months of 2026.

4
00:00:06,560 --> 00:00:07,830
Not fifty-nine a week.

5
00:00:07,880 --> 00:00:09,100
Not fifty-nine a month.

6
00:00:09,150 --> 00:00:13,210
Fifty-nine in nine months, across a
country of twenty-seven million people.

7
00:00:13,260 --> 00:00:14,590
In the same nine months,

8
00:00:14,640 --> 00:00:17,450
Toyota sold more than nine
thousand four hundred Camrys.

9
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:21,050
That's over one hundred and sixty
Camrys for every single Accord.

10
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:22,590
And the Accord is not alone.

11
00:00:22,640 --> 00:00:25,410
A seven-seat Kia that costs close
to a hundred thousand dollars.

12
00:00:25,460 --> 00:00:29,050
A Ford with a famous badge that's been
cut by up to nine and a half thousand

13
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:31,730
dollars and still can't find buyers.

14
00:00:31,780 --> 00:00:35,330
A Skoda that the RAV4 outsells by
more than a hundred and thirty to one.

15
00:00:35,380 --> 00:00:39,750
And one brand that has not one, not
two, but three cars on this list.

16
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:40,900
Here's the crazy part.

17
00:00:40,950 --> 00:00:43,590
Australians are buying
more new cars than ever.

18
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:46,870
October 2026 was the
biggest October in history.

19
00:00:46,920 --> 00:00:48,530
So buyers haven't disappeared.

20
00:00:48,580 --> 00:00:51,010
They've just walked straight
past these ten cars.

21
00:00:51,060 --> 00:00:51,870
So in this video,

22
00:00:51,920 --> 00:00:56,410
I'm counting down the ten new cars
Australians are refusing to buy in 2026

23
00:00:56,460 --> 00:00:58,710
with the real sales numbers, the prices,

24
00:00:58,760 --> 00:01:01,850
and the desperate moves brands
are making to shift them.

25
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:02,830
Stay to the end,

26
00:01:02,880 --> 00:01:05,890
because I'll also show you the cars
that sold just one or two units last

27
00:01:05,940 --> 00:01:09,180
month, and how to turn all of this
into a better deal for yourself.

28
00:01:09,807 --> 00:01:13,287
First, the big picture, because it
explains everything on this list.

29
00:01:13,337 --> 00:01:19,377
Australians bought 107,493
new vehicles in October 2026,

30
00:01:19,427 --> 00:01:21,717
according to the official VFACTS figures.

31
00:01:21,767 --> 00:01:26,057
That's up 6.8 per cent on October
last year, and a record for the month.

32
00:01:26,107 --> 00:01:29,477
Year to date, the market has
already passed one million sales.

33
00:01:29,527 --> 00:01:31,257
But look at where that money is going.

34
00:01:31,307 --> 00:01:35,477
Electric car sales were up 237
per cent on October last year.

35
00:01:35,527 --> 00:01:38,657
BYD sold more than ten thousand
cars in a single month,

36
00:01:38,707 --> 00:01:40,337
up 153 per cent,

37
00:01:40,387 --> 00:01:43,217
and it's now firmly the second
biggest brand in the country,

38
00:01:43,267 --> 00:01:45,037
behind only Toyota.

39
00:01:45,087 --> 00:01:46,937
Geely was up 520 per cent.

40
00:01:46,987 --> 00:01:49,817
Cars built in China were up 104 per cent.

41
00:01:49,867 --> 00:01:51,997
Now look at who's going backwards.

42
00:01:52,047 --> 00:01:54,477
Mitsubishi, down 50
per cent for the month.

43
00:01:54,527 --> 00:01:56,917
Volkswagen, down 46.

44
00:01:56,967 --> 00:01:58,617
Audi, down 45.

45
00:01:58,667 --> 00:02:00,517
Subaru, down 42.

46
00:02:00,567 --> 00:02:02,917
Hyundai, down almost 29.

47
00:02:02,967 --> 00:02:04,537
Mazda, down almost 20.

48
00:02:04,587 --> 00:02:06,877
Cars from Japan were down 13 per cent,

49
00:02:06,927 --> 00:02:11,097
from Korea down 23, and
from Germany down 24.

50
00:02:11,147 --> 00:02:12,917
So this isn't a weak market.

51
00:02:12,967 --> 00:02:16,917
It's a market where buyers are moving
fast and when buyers move this fast,

52
00:02:16,967 --> 00:02:19,557
some cars get left behind
in the dealer's yard.

53
00:02:19,607 --> 00:02:21,797
A quick word on how I built this list.

54
00:02:21,847 --> 00:02:26,277
The ranking uses year-to-date sales
from January to September 2026,

55
00:02:26,327 --> 00:02:29,077
compared with the same
nine months of 2025,

56
00:02:29,127 --> 00:02:32,677
as compiled by GoAuto from
the official VFACTS data.

57
00:02:32,727 --> 00:02:36,737
I've added October numbers from
CarExpert's sales database where they help.

58
00:02:36,787 --> 00:02:39,057
And I've only included cars
that are still on sale.

59
00:02:39,107 --> 00:02:42,117
Cars that have already been
axed are a different story,

60
00:02:42,167 --> 00:02:43,897
and I'll deal with those separately.

61
00:02:43,947 --> 00:02:45,087
Let's start the countdown.

62
00:02:46,870 --> 00:02:50,258
Number ten: the KGM Rexton.

63
00:02:50,308 --> 00:02:51,818
The Rexton is a big, rugged,

64
00:02:51,868 --> 00:02:55,538
diesel four-wheel-drive seven-seater
from the brand Australians used to know

65
00:02:55,588 --> 00:02:56,538
as SsangYong.

66
00:02:56,588 --> 00:02:58,758
It's built for towing and for the bush,

67
00:02:58,808 --> 00:03:02,078
and it's priced from about fifty-two
thousand dollars drive-away up to just

68
00:03:02,128 --> 00:03:04,698
over sixty-four thousand
for the top model.

69
00:03:04,748 --> 00:03:08,778
On paper, that's great value against
a Toyota Prado or a Ford Everest.

70
00:03:08,828 --> 00:03:10,138
But look at the numbers.

71
00:03:10,188 --> 00:03:15,258
In the first nine months of 2026,
the Rexton found 371 buyers.

72
00:03:15,308 --> 00:03:19,398
In the same period last
year, it was 1,125.

73
00:03:19,448 --> 00:03:21,218
That's a fall of 67 per cent.

74
00:03:21,268 --> 00:03:22,768
By the end of October,

75
00:03:22,818 --> 00:03:26,538
CarExpert's database had the
Rexton on 403 for the year,

76
00:03:26,588 --> 00:03:28,018
still down two thirds.

77
00:03:28,068 --> 00:03:29,638
GoAuto put it brutally.

78
00:03:29,688 --> 00:03:31,638
Of all the slow sellers it looked at,

79
00:03:31,688 --> 00:03:35,698
the Rexton has "the dubious honour" of
both the highest sales and the steepest

80
00:03:35,748 --> 00:03:36,598
decline.

81
00:03:36,648 --> 00:03:39,338
And while the Rexton sold 371,

82
00:03:39,388 --> 00:03:46,888
the Ford Everest sold more than sixteen

83
00:03:58,241 --> 00:04:05,741
thousand.

84
00:04:06,968 --> 00:04:10,736
That's almost forty-four
Everests for every Rexton.

85
00:04:10,786 --> 00:04:17,438
Part of the problem is the price climb.

86
00:04:17,488 --> 00:04:22,258
For 2026, the Rexton got more equipment
but it also got more expensive.

87
00:04:22,308 --> 00:04:23,438
And at the same time,

88
00:04:23,488 --> 00:04:26,788
Chinese brands have flooded this
exact part of the market with cheaper

89
00:04:26,838 --> 00:04:29,678
seven-seat SUVs and plug-in hybrids.

90
00:04:29,728 --> 00:04:32,438
When the value brand stops
being the cheapest option,

91
00:04:32,488 --> 00:04:34,808
buyers start asking why
they should take the risk.

92
00:04:35,638 --> 00:04:37,808
Number nine: the Skoda Octavia.

93
00:04:37,858 --> 00:04:41,008
This is the first of
three Skodas on this list,

94
00:04:41,058 --> 00:04:43,028
and that tells you something already.

95
00:04:43,078 --> 00:04:46,868
The Octavia is a car that motoring
journalists have loved for years.

96
00:04:46,918 --> 00:04:49,888
It's practical, it's well
built, it drives nicely,

97
00:04:49,938 --> 00:04:53,168
and the wagon is one of the most
useful family cars you can buy.

98
00:04:53,218 --> 00:04:57,888
In 2026, Skoda even added a new
mild-hybrid version to the range.

99
00:04:57,938 --> 00:04:59,368
But buyers aren't listening.

100
00:04:59,418 --> 00:05:03,468
The Octavia sold 340 cars in the
first nine months of the year,

101
00:05:03,518 --> 00:05:07,768
down from 557 in the same period of 2025.

102
00:05:07,818 --> 00:05:09,568
That's a fall of 39 per cent.

103
00:05:09,618 --> 00:05:12,068
Prices start at around forty-three and
a half thousand dollars drive-away,

104
00:05:12,118 --> 00:05:16,088
and the hot RS goes past
sixty-five thousand.

105
00:05:16,138 --> 00:05:17,728
Here's the comparison that hurts.

106
00:05:17,778 --> 00:05:22,528
In the same segment, the
Toyota Camry sold 9,471.

107
00:05:22,578 --> 00:05:25,408
That's almost twenty-eight
Camrys for every Octavia.

108
00:05:25,458 --> 00:05:27,808
The problem isn't that
the Octavia is a bad car.

109
00:05:27,858 --> 00:05:30,888
It's that it's a petrol
car, a European car,

110
00:05:30,938 --> 00:05:34,948
and a sedan or wagon three things the
Australian market is moving away from at

111
00:05:34,998 --> 00:05:36,328
the same time.

112
00:05:36,378 --> 00:05:39,768
Buyers who want something
practical are buying hybrid SUVs.

113
00:05:39,818 --> 00:05:43,108
Buyers who want something new are
walking into Chinese showrooms.

114
00:05:43,158 --> 00:05:44,938
And the Octavia is stuck in the middle.

115
00:05:45,746 --> 00:05:47,536
Number eight: the Jeep Wrangler.

116
00:05:47,586 --> 00:05:49,636
The Wrangler is an icon.

117
00:05:49,686 --> 00:05:53,316
It's the original off-roader, and
you can spot one from a mile away.

118
00:05:53,366 --> 00:05:56,056
But in the first nine months of 2026,

119
00:05:56,106 --> 00:05:58,496
Australians bought just 247 of them,

120
00:05:58,546 --> 00:06:02,056
down from 345 in the
same period last year.

121
00:06:02,106 --> 00:06:04,036
That's a fall of more than 28 per cent.

122
00:06:04,086 --> 00:06:05,836
Price is the big issue.

123
00:06:05,886 --> 00:06:08,996
The cheapest four-door Wrangler went
from around thirty-seven thousand dollars

124
00:06:09,046 --> 00:06:13,596
back in 2014 to almost seventy-six
thousand before on-road costs.

125
00:06:13,646 --> 00:06:16,796
At that money, buyers are
cross-shopping a Prado,

126
00:06:16,846 --> 00:06:20,576
an Everest, or a Chinese four-by-four
with a lot more equipment.

127
00:06:20,626 --> 00:06:24,446
GoAuto worked out that the Ford Everest
outsold the Wrangler by more than

128
00:06:24,496 --> 00:06:26,056
sixty-five to one this year.

129
00:06:26,106 --> 00:06:28,096
And look at the rest of the Jeep showroom.

130
00:06:28,146 --> 00:06:30,776
In October, the Jeep Compass sold one car.

131
00:06:30,826 --> 00:06:31,436
One.

132
00:06:31,486 --> 00:06:34,276
The Grand Cherokee and
the Avenger sold zero.

133
00:06:34,326 --> 00:06:38,036
Right now, Jeep is offering a
four-thousand-dollar deposit contribution on the

134
00:06:38,086 --> 00:06:41,756
Wrangler Rubicon four-door, according
to the deals tracker CarSorted.

135
00:06:41,806 --> 00:06:44,116
When a brand starts paying
part of your deposit,

136
00:06:44,166 --> 00:06:46,306
that tells you how hard
the cars are to move.

137
00:06:47,900 --> 00:06:49,158
Number seven: the Skoda Karoq.

138
00:06:49,208 --> 00:06:50,518
Skoda number two.

139
00:06:50,568 --> 00:06:52,938
The Karoq is a sensible mid-size SUV,

140
00:06:52,988 --> 00:06:56,098
and CarExpert rated it "very
good" in a recent review,

141
00:06:56,148 --> 00:06:57,578
praising its easy driving,

142
00:06:57,628 --> 00:07:03,638
low servicing costs and sharp drive-away
pricing from $40,990 drive-away.

143
00:07:03,688 --> 00:07:06,058
But the sales chart tells a sad story.

144
00:07:06,108 --> 00:07:09,778
The Karoq sold 752 cars in 2024.

145
00:07:09,828 --> 00:07:12,498
Then 470 in 2025.

146
00:07:12,548 --> 00:07:14,658
And in the first nine months of 2026,

147
00:07:14,708 --> 00:07:19,378
just 232, down 32 per cent
on the same period last year.

148
00:07:19,428 --> 00:07:20,618
To put that in perspective,

149
00:07:20,668 --> 00:07:26,018
it's in the same segment as the Toyota
RAV4 Australia's best-selling SUV.

150
00:07:26,068 --> 00:07:29,954
GoAuto worked out that the RAV4 is
outselling the Karoq by almost one hundred

151
00:07:30,004 --> 00:07:31,591
and thirty-five to one.

152
00:07:31,641 --> 00:07:35,658
CarExpert's review even pointed out
that the Karoq is being outsold by newer

153
00:07:35,708 --> 00:07:38,738
or niche cars like the Deepal S07,

154
00:07:38,788 --> 00:07:42,158
the Skoda Elroq, the Mini
Countryman and the Volvo EX30.

155
00:07:42,208 --> 00:07:44,838
The reviewer's verdict was revealing too:

156
00:07:44,888 --> 00:07:47,858
underpowered, a tight back
seat, some dated tech,

157
00:07:47,908 --> 00:07:49,818
and a car that "feels like a rental".

158
00:07:49,868 --> 00:07:53,378
That's exactly the kind of car that
gets crushed when buyers have dozens of

159
00:07:53,428 --> 00:07:57,328
shiny new hybrids and electric SUVs
to choose from at the same money.

160
00:07:58,066 --> 00:08:00,876
Number six: the Ford Mustang Mach-E.

161
00:08:00,926 --> 00:08:03,196
This one might be the
strangest on the list.

162
00:08:03,246 --> 00:08:05,736
It has one of the most
famous badges in the world.

163
00:08:05,786 --> 00:08:07,216
It's an electric SUV,

164
00:08:07,266 --> 00:08:10,496
in a year when electric car
sales in Australia are exploding.

165
00:08:10,546 --> 00:08:12,136
And yet, nobody wants it.

166
00:08:12,186 --> 00:08:16,616
The Mach-E sold 206 cars in
the first nine months of 2026,

167
00:08:16,666 --> 00:08:19,936
down more than 34 per cent
on the same period last year.

168
00:08:19,986 --> 00:08:23,776
In 2025, it found fewer than
five hundred buyers in total.

169
00:08:23,826 --> 00:08:25,496
And it's not for lack of trying.

170
00:08:25,546 --> 00:08:27,336
Ford has already cut the price.

171
00:08:27,386 --> 00:08:30,916
EV Central reported drive-away offers
of sixty thousand dollars for the

172
00:08:30,966 --> 00:08:34,796
Select, seventy-five thousand for the
Premium and eighty-nine thousand for the

173
00:08:34,846 --> 00:08:38,636
GT cuts of up to around nine and a half
thousand dollars on the earlier list

174
00:08:38,686 --> 00:08:39,576
prices.

175
00:08:39,626 --> 00:08:43,116
That reviewer described the price cuts
as a sign that Ford was "desperate to

176
00:08:43,166 --> 00:08:44,216
shift" stock.

177
00:08:44,266 --> 00:08:45,636
Compare that with America,

178
00:08:45,686 --> 00:08:49,376
where Ford sold more than
fifty thousand Mach-Es in 2025.

179
00:08:49,426 --> 00:08:51,316
So why is Australia so different?

180
00:08:51,366 --> 00:08:52,856
Simple: competition.

181
00:08:52,906 --> 00:08:56,196
In Australia, a Mach-E is
fighting the Tesla Model Y,

182
00:08:56,246 --> 00:08:58,056
the BYD Sealion 7,

183
00:08:58,106 --> 00:09:03,136
the Geely EX5 and a dozen other electric
SUVs, many of them cheaper and newer.

184
00:09:03,186 --> 00:09:07,396
In October alone, the
Model Y sold 3,105 cars.

185
00:09:07,446 --> 00:09:10,066
The Mach-E sold 206 in nine months.

186
00:09:11,831 --> 00:09:13,676
Number five: the Mazda CX-70.

187
00:09:13,726 --> 00:09:15,836
The CX-70 is Mazda's big,

188
00:09:15,886 --> 00:09:19,656
premium five-seat SUV, with a
powerful straight-six engine.

189
00:09:19,706 --> 00:09:23,536
It's built for the American market and
in Australia, it has never caught on.

190
00:09:23,586 --> 00:09:27,936
It sold 182 cars in the
first nine months of 2026,

191
00:09:27,986 --> 00:09:31,496
down from 278 in the
same period last year.

192
00:09:31,546 --> 00:09:34,031
That's a fall of almost 35 per cent.

193
00:09:34,081 --> 00:09:37,976
GoAuto noted that in the large SUV
class above eighty thousand dollars,

194
00:09:38,026 --> 00:09:44,376
the Land Rover Defender sold 3,098 that's
seventeen Defenders for every CX-70.

195
00:09:44,426 --> 00:09:46,876
And this is despite a major price cut.

196
00:09:46,926 --> 00:09:48,716
In July 2026,

197
00:09:48,766 --> 00:09:54,716
Mazda slashed CX-70 prices
by between $3,700 and $8,051,

198
00:09:54,766 --> 00:09:56,096
depending on the variant.

199
00:09:56,146 --> 00:09:57,616
It didn't fix the problem.

200
00:09:57,666 --> 00:09:59,176
Then in late October,

201
00:09:59,226 --> 00:10:03,376
Mazda confirmed the CX-70 is ending
production for the United States its

202
00:10:03,426 --> 00:10:04,716
biggest market.

203
00:10:04,766 --> 00:10:06,996
Mazda Australia says the
car will continue here,

204
00:10:07,046 --> 00:10:10,036
and that it still has a
small but loyal fanbase.

205
00:10:10,086 --> 00:10:13,896
But when a car is built mainly for
America and America no longer gets it,

206
00:10:13,946 --> 00:10:16,946
buyers here will be asking how
long it's really going to last.

207
00:10:17,808 --> 00:10:19,898
Number four: the Hyundai Sonata.

208
00:10:19,948 --> 00:10:21,498
Here's a car whose sales are collapsing,

209
00:10:21,548 --> 00:10:24,718
and Hyundai's response
is… to put the price up.

210
00:10:24,768 --> 00:10:29,038
In Australia, the Sonata is now sold
only as the sporty N Line sedan.

211
00:10:29,088 --> 00:10:33,918
It found just 179 buyers in
the first nine months of 2026,

212
00:10:33,968 --> 00:10:37,198
down 37 per cent on the
same period last year.

213
00:10:37,248 --> 00:10:40,978
The Toyota Camry outsold it
by almost fifty-three to one.

214
00:10:41,028 --> 00:10:42,998
And then, from the first of October,

215
00:10:43,048 --> 00:10:45,738
Hyundai raised the Sonata N Line's
price by five hundred dollars,

216
00:10:45,788 --> 00:10:49,918
to fifty-seven thousand
dollars before on-road costs.

217
00:10:49,968 --> 00:10:52,698
That's more than sixty-one
thousand drive-away in Sydney.

218
00:10:52,748 --> 00:10:55,208
Why would you raise the price
of a car that isn't selling?

219
00:10:55,258 --> 00:10:57,838
Hyundai blamed "global economic factors,

220
00:10:57,888 --> 00:11:00,778
manufacturing, logistics
and local policy".

221
00:11:00,828 --> 00:11:04,398
That local policy is Australia's
New Vehicle Efficiency Standard,

222
00:11:04,448 --> 00:11:07,618
which sets limits on
average CO2 emissions.

223
00:11:07,668 --> 00:11:08,818
According to reports,

224
00:11:08,868 --> 00:11:12,958
Hyundai was fined 4.2 million
dollars for missing its 2025 target,

225
00:11:13,008 --> 00:11:17,278
and the targets get
tougher in 2026 and 2027.

226
00:11:17,328 --> 00:11:20,938
A big petrol sedan doesn't help
Hyundai's numbers so there's very little

227
00:11:20,988 --> 00:11:22,618
reason for it to discount one.

228
00:11:22,668 --> 00:11:24,958
And the bigger picture
for Hyundai is ugly.

229
00:11:25,008 --> 00:11:28,278
In October, the whole brand
was down almost 29 per cent.

230
00:11:28,328 --> 00:11:31,608
Its sister brand Kia is now
outselling it for the year.

231
00:11:32,320 --> 00:11:34,870
Number three: the Skoda Fabia.

232
00:11:34,920 --> 00:11:36,070
Skoda number three.

233
00:11:36,120 --> 00:11:39,750
And yes, that means one brand
has three cars in this top ten.

234
00:11:39,800 --> 00:11:43,770
The Fabia is Skoda's smallest
car, a little European hatchback.

235
00:11:43,820 --> 00:11:47,830
It sold 140 cars in the
first nine months of 2026,

236
00:11:47,880 --> 00:11:51,230
down from 246 in the
same period last year.

237
00:11:51,280 --> 00:11:52,830
That's a fall of 43 per cent.

238
00:11:52,880 --> 00:11:54,950
Now look at the car
that's eating its lunch.

239
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:59,050
In the light car segment,
the MG3 sold 6,340.

240
00:11:59,100 --> 00:12:02,990
That's more than forty-five
MG3s for every Fabia.

241
00:12:03,040 --> 00:12:06,570
A cheap Chinese-made hybrid hatch has
completely taken over the space that

242
00:12:06,620 --> 00:12:08,590
European small cars used to own.

243
00:12:08,640 --> 00:12:10,230
And the Skoda pattern goes further.

244
00:12:10,280 --> 00:12:14,890
In October, the Skoda Superb one of the
roomiest cars you can buy sold nine.

245
00:12:14,940 --> 00:12:17,710
The Skoda Scala small hatch sold zero.

246
00:12:17,760 --> 00:12:20,950
Skoda's sister brand Volkswagen
was down 46 per cent for the month,

247
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:23,190
and Cupra was down 67.

248
00:12:23,240 --> 00:12:24,410
To be fair to Skoda,

249
00:12:24,460 --> 00:12:28,670
it's pushing new models like the
Elroq electric SUV and new hybrids.

250
00:12:28,720 --> 00:12:29,570
But right now,

251
00:12:29,620 --> 00:12:33,540
the old guard of European small cars is
getting crushed from every direction.

252
00:12:34,406 --> 00:12:37,016
Number two: the Kia EV9.

253
00:12:37,066 --> 00:12:39,396
This is the most
expensive car on the list.

254
00:12:39,446 --> 00:12:43,136
The Kia EV9 is a big,
seven-seat electric SUV,

255
00:12:43,186 --> 00:12:49,516
and in 2026 Kia added a new
GT version priced at $129,250

256
00:12:49,566 --> 00:12:52,196
the most expensive Kia
ever sold in Australia.

257
00:12:52,246 --> 00:12:56,236
The range starts at $97,000
before on-road costs.

258
00:12:56,286 --> 00:13:00,456
And here's how many Australians bought
one in the first nine months of 2026:

259
00:13:00,506 --> 00:13:01,396
120.

260
00:13:01,446 --> 00:13:06,529
That's down from 238 in the same period
last year a drop of almost 50 per

261
00:13:06,579 --> 00:13:06,836
cent.

262
00:13:06,886 --> 00:13:09,176
Half the buyers, gone in a year.

263
00:13:09,226 --> 00:13:11,976
GoAuto compared it with the
biggest seller in its class,

264
00:13:12,026 --> 00:13:16,496
the Toyota LandCruiser
300, which sold 9,787.

265
00:13:16,546 --> 00:13:19,876
That's more than eighty-one
LandCruisers for every EV9.

266
00:13:19,926 --> 00:13:21,276
So what went wrong?

267
00:13:21,326 --> 00:13:24,536
Electric car sales are booming but
they're booming at the cheaper end.

268
00:13:24,586 --> 00:13:28,436
The best-selling EVs are thirty,
forty and fifty thousand dollar cars.

269
00:13:28,486 --> 00:13:32,416
A hundred-thousand-dollar electric
family bus is a very small market,

270
00:13:32,466 --> 00:13:35,636
and it's now shared with Chinese
seven-seaters that cost a fraction of the

271
00:13:35,686 --> 00:13:36,076
price.

272
00:13:36,126 --> 00:13:41,156
And remember, the Hyundai Ioniq 9 the
EV9's sister under the skin sold just

273
00:13:41,206 --> 00:13:42,646
four cars in October.

274
00:13:44,508 --> 00:13:45,991
And number one: the Honda Accord.

275
00:13:46,041 --> 00:13:47,331
The car we started with.

276
00:13:47,381 --> 00:13:50,851
Fifty-nine sales in the
first nine months of 2026,

277
00:13:50,901 --> 00:13:53,791
down from 78 in the same period last year.

278
00:13:53,841 --> 00:13:57,131
That's fewer than seven cars a
month, across the entire country.

279
00:13:57,181 --> 00:13:59,911
The Accord is now sold here
as a single hybrid model,

280
00:13:59,961 --> 00:14:04,851
the e:HEV RS, at around
$64,900 drive-away.

281
00:14:04,901 --> 00:14:06,691
That's a lot of money
for a mid-size sedan,

282
00:14:06,741 --> 00:14:09,711
in a market that is falling
out of love with sedans.

283
00:14:09,761 --> 00:14:14,481
For comparison, a Toyota Camry hybrid
starts at much less and Toyota sold

284
00:14:14,531 --> 00:14:16,891
9,471 of them.

285
00:14:16,941 --> 00:14:20,051
That's over one hundred and
sixty Camrys for every Accord.

286
00:14:20,101 --> 00:14:22,991
Honda's business model in
Australia is part of the story.

287
00:14:23,041 --> 00:14:26,084
Since 2021, Honda has
sold its cars at fixed,

288
00:14:26,134 --> 00:14:28,791
no-haggle drive-away prices
through an agency model,

289
00:14:28,841 --> 00:14:30,811
with far fewer dealerships.

290
00:14:30,861 --> 00:14:32,211
It said it wanted fewer,

291
00:14:32,261 --> 00:14:36,091
more profitable sales and with the
Accord, it certainly has fewer.

292
00:14:36,141 --> 00:14:37,911
And now Honda is trying to move them.

293
00:14:37,961 --> 00:14:41,031
Its end-of-year plate clearance includes
a thousand-dollar gift card on the

294
00:14:41,081 --> 00:14:44,084
Accord hybrid, plus the
first five services free.

295
00:14:44,134 --> 00:14:48,691
Meanwhile, CarExpert reported that
the updated 2027 Accord will cost a

296
00:14:48,741 --> 00:14:50,111
thousand dollars more.

297
00:14:50,161 --> 00:14:52,911
GoAuto made an important
point about this whole list:

298
00:14:52,961 --> 00:14:55,531
these sales gaps aren't
necessarily about product quality.

299
00:14:55,581 --> 00:14:56,811
And that's true.

300
00:14:56,861 --> 00:14:58,371
The Accord is a good car.

301
00:14:58,421 --> 00:15:01,941
It just costs too much, in a body
style Australians are abandoning.

302
00:15:02,873 --> 00:15:03,803
Before we finish,

303
00:15:03,853 --> 00:15:06,803
let's look at October because some
of the monthly numbers are even more

304
00:15:06,853 --> 00:15:08,403
shocking than the countdown.

305
00:15:08,453 --> 00:15:10,743
According to CarExpert's sales database,

306
00:15:10,793 --> 00:15:13,883
88 models recorded zero sales in October.

307
00:15:13,933 --> 00:15:15,243
Now, to be fair,

308
00:15:15,293 --> 00:15:18,743
many of those are cars that have
been axed or are between generations.

309
00:15:18,793 --> 00:15:22,403
But some of the low numbers are on
cars that are very much still on sale.

310
00:15:22,453 --> 00:15:26,983
The Audi Q4 e-tron: two sales
in October, down 96 per cent.

311
00:15:27,033 --> 00:15:30,618
Audi has now cut the price of the
updated model by up to eighteen thousand

312
00:15:30,668 --> 00:15:34,903
dollars, to get it under the luxury car
tax threshold but deliveries of that

313
00:15:34,953 --> 00:15:36,803
model don't start until 2027.

314
00:15:36,853 --> 00:15:41,983
The BMW iX electric SUV:
four sales, down 86 per cent.

315
00:15:42,033 --> 00:15:46,143
The Hyundai Ioniq 9
seven-seat electric SUV: four.

316
00:15:46,193 --> 00:15:49,603
The Suzuki S-Cross: two,
down almost 90 per cent.

317
00:15:49,653 --> 00:15:53,363
The Renault Kangoo van:
two, down almost 97.

318
00:15:53,413 --> 00:15:55,383
The Fiat 500: three.

319
00:15:55,433 --> 00:15:57,643
The Peugeot 308: three.

320
00:15:57,693 --> 00:16:01,403
And the Alfa Romeo Tonale: one
single car, down 80 per cent.

321
00:16:01,453 --> 00:16:04,813
And here's one that looks like a
disaster, but isn't quite what it seems.

322
00:16:04,863 --> 00:16:08,383
The Toyota Fortuner sold
just eight cars in October,

323
00:16:08,433 --> 00:16:10,143
down more than 97 per cent.

324
00:16:10,193 --> 00:16:14,043
But that's because Toyota has axed
it in Australia, with no replacement.

325
00:16:14,093 --> 00:16:16,223
Dealers are simply selling the last ones.

326
00:16:16,273 --> 00:16:18,053
That's why it isn't in my top ten.

327
00:16:18,822 --> 00:16:20,812
So what does all this mean for you?

328
00:16:20,862 --> 00:16:24,592
If you're buying, cars that aren't
selling are where the biggest deals live.

329
00:16:24,642 --> 00:16:26,392
When a model sits in a dealer's yard,

330
00:16:26,442 --> 00:16:28,452
it costs the dealer money every week,

331
00:16:28,502 --> 00:16:31,272
and the end of the year is when
dealers are chasing their targets.

332
00:16:31,322 --> 00:16:33,412
If one of these cars genuinely suits you,

333
00:16:33,462 --> 00:16:35,472
ask for a drive-away price in writing,

334
00:16:35,522 --> 00:16:37,452
ask how long that car has been in stock,

335
00:16:37,502 --> 00:16:39,892
and ask whether a newer
model is on the way.

336
00:16:39,942 --> 00:16:43,092
Old stock and demonstrators are where
dealers usually have the most room to

337
00:16:43,142 --> 00:16:43,772
move.

338
00:16:43,822 --> 00:16:44,412
But be careful.

339
00:16:44,462 --> 00:16:48,672
A car that's hard to sell new is
usually hard to sell used, too.

340
00:16:48,722 --> 00:16:51,992
Expect faster depreciation,
and plan to keep it longer.

341
00:16:52,042 --> 00:16:53,832
Check the warranty, the service plan,

342
00:16:53,882 --> 00:16:57,252
and how far you'll have to travel for
parts and servicing especially with

343
00:16:57,302 --> 00:16:58,572
smaller brands.

344
00:16:58,622 --> 00:17:01,612
And if you already own one
of these cars, don't panic.

345
00:17:01,662 --> 00:17:05,512
Low new-car sales don't change your
warranty or your consumer rights.

346
00:17:05,562 --> 00:17:07,292
Keep your service history up to date,

347
00:17:07,342 --> 00:17:08,652
and if you're thinking of selling,

348
00:17:08,702 --> 00:17:11,732
get several valuations before
you accept a trade-in offer.

349
00:17:11,782 --> 00:17:13,032
So that's the list.

350
00:17:13,082 --> 00:17:15,872
The KGM Rexton, the Skoda Octavia,

351
00:17:15,922 --> 00:17:17,652
the Jeep Wrangler, the Skoda Karoq,

352
00:17:17,702 --> 00:17:20,952
the Ford Mustang Mach-E, the Mazda CX-70,

353
00:17:21,002 --> 00:17:24,532
the Hyundai Sonata, the
Skoda Fabia, the Kia EV9,

354
00:17:24,582 --> 00:17:28,452
and at number one, the Honda Accord
fifty-nine sales in nine months.

355
00:17:28,502 --> 00:17:29,892
Now I want to hear from you.

356
00:17:29,942 --> 00:17:33,572
Which car on this list would you
actually buy, if the price was right?

357
00:17:33,622 --> 00:17:34,912
Tell me in the comments.

358
00:17:34,962 --> 00:17:37,412
If you found this useful,
hit like and subscribe,

359
00:17:37,462 --> 00:17:40,992
because in the next video I'm counting
down the biggest new-car discounts in

360
00:17:41,042 --> 00:17:44,732
Australia right now including one ute
that's more than ten thousand dollars

361
00:17:44,782 --> 00:17:46,092
cheaper than it was.

362
00:17:46,142 --> 00:17:46,942
See you there.
